# Handbook Charter Intake

Use this skill only inside a real git work tree. The installed CLI owns immutable lineage, native-authority decisions, promotion, canonical YAML, and rendered review views.

Resolve the installed runtime first:

```bash
repo_root="$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null)" || {
  echo "REFUSED: run this skill from inside a real git repository." >&2
  exit 1
}
handbook_home="${HANDBOOK_HOME:-$HOME/handbook}"
for required in \
  "$handbook_home/bin/handbook" \
  "$handbook_home/runtime-manifest.json" \
  "$handbook_home/resources/authoring/charter_authoring_method.md" \
  "$handbook_home/resources/charter/CHARTER_INPUTS.yaml.tmpl" \
  "$handbook_home/resources/charter/charter_inputs_directive.md"; do
  [[ -f "$required" ]] || {
    echo "REFUSED: missing installed handbook home prerequisite: $required" >&2
    exit 1
  }
done
export HANDBOOK_HOME="$handbook_home"
cd "$repo_root"
```

Choose exactly one acquisition mode and prepare one closed, typed intake envelope outside the repository. Gather evidenced repository facts; record unknowns and contradictions in the envelope instead of inventing answers. The workflow has no secondary model invocation or CLI questionnaire.

- `handbook author charter --mode guided-adaptive --from-inputs <path|->`
- `handbook author charter --mode express --from-inputs <path|->`
- `handbook author charter --mode agent-assisted --from-inputs <path|->`

Successful acquisition creates immutable intake and candidate lineage only. It does not select canonical truth. Present the candidate reference, fingerprint, rendered review view, unresolved unknowns, contradictions, and required approval classes to the user.

The candidate requires human approval as an explicit later action through native authority:

- `handbook author charter --approve-candidate <candidate-ref> --approval-class <class> --authority-ref <authority-ref>`

After all required approvals exist, promote the exact approved candidate:

- `handbook author charter --promote-candidate <candidate-ref> --approval-ref <approval-ref>`

Validate selected canonical truth without mutation:

- `handbook author charter --validate`

Use `--json` for machine-readable results. Honor every typed refusal and next action. Never edit canonical Charter YAML or rendered Markdown directly, never self-approve, and never infer an authority reference.

Repo-local `.agents/skills/handbook*` trees are generated discovery projections, not the runtime payload root.
